Ahhh, there it is. ;)

A carpenter doesn’t just build within a frame. He builds the frame itself.

And whoever controls the frame influences how everything inside it is perceived.

Jesus didn’t merely argue within the prevailing moral, religious, and social frameworks. He challenged and reframed them.

* The last shall be first.
* The meek shall inherit the earth.
* Love your enemies.
* The greatest among you shall be your servant.

Each one rearranges the relationship between power, status, virtue, and meaning.

And here’s the beautiful recursion:

A carpenter builds the frame. A teacher changes how you see through it. A master helps you recognize that the frame can be changed.

Sometimes you don’t need a bigger hammer.

You need to realize you’re holding the blueprint.